      "value": "@{5ce2ec6dfd8fa55a6d3a1973|full_name}: \n> be the first in it\n\nThat's different thing tho, worlds have owner and master (not sure if owner is official term in any way), tho I think that currently public worlds do not have owner (or it was creator of given world maybe? i dont remember), but I guess that the point of this feature request.\nOwner is the person who created the instance, so person that clicked that new world button.\nMaster is that internal thing used for maintaining network sync/authority, but also used for few other things, like often people make some buttons usable only to master to prevent multiple people using it, as there is always some master in the room, while owner could just quit. In most cases master is the first person to join and later it goes to the next person if master will leave the instance.\n\nso IMHO everyone should be able to vote to kick the master, but not the owner.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-17T09:58:22.245Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it currently stands the kick system is highly abuseable and I feel it requires a revamp.\n\nMy suggestions start off with Room Master's should not be able to get Vote Kicked from their instance. No matter how cancerous they are it's their room- leave it or deal with it. Any extremities can be reported/logged.\n\nAs the system currently stands the current kicks will be won at 50% vote rate,  \n2 people = 1 vote = 100%,\n3 people = 1 vote = 50%\n4 people = 2 vote = 66%\n5 people = 3 vote = 60%\nfor every person in the room, 1 is subtracted for the one being kicked- they have no vote. the above is based on minimum votes.\n\nThis system is abusable. and should be more controlled.\n\nAlternative suggestions: allow the primary kicker to provide a reason. When done forward the final vote tally and reason to the room master who can finalize the kick or not.",
